config MESHTASTIC_OTA
	bool "Firmware update into the MCUboot second slot over SMP (mcumgr)"
	depends on BOOTLOADER_MCUBOOT
	select MCUMGR
	select NET_BUF          # mcumgr core dependency
	select ZCBOR            # mcumgr core dependency
	select CRC              # SMP framing checksum
	select MCUMGR_GRP_IMG
	select MCUMGR_GRP_OS
	select IMG_MANAGER
	select STREAM_FLASH
	help
	  Run an mcumgr SMP server so the node can be updated into the MCUboot
	  slot1 partition (image upload -> test -> reset -> swap -> confirm), with
	  automatic MCUboot revert if a swapped image is never confirmed. Requires
	  the MCUboot A/B build (sysbuild).

	  This symbol is the SUBSYSTEM only — it deliberately selects no transport.
	  The transport is chosen by the overlay that enables it, because it is the
	  only part of the update path that depends on what radio a board has:
	    overlay-ota.conf        SMP over UDP (WiFi boards; the net profiles)
	    overlay-ota-shell.conf  SMP over the shell's serial console (any board
	                            with a console; the XIAO's USB CDC)
	  A BLE transport (MCUMGR_TRANSPORT_BT) goes beside them. The transports
	  self-start, so no application code is required for the core update path.

if MESHTASTIC_OTA

config MESHTASTIC_OTA_AUTOCONFIRM
	bool "Auto-confirm the running image after a healthy delay"
	default n
	help
	  After MESHTASTIC_OTA_CONFIRM_DELAY_SEC of healthy uptime, call
	  boot_write_img_confirmed() so a freshly-swapped image becomes permanent
	  without a manual `mcumgr image confirm`. Leave OFF for the safest story:
	  an unconfirmed image is reverted by MCUboot on the next unexpected reset.

config MESHTASTIC_OTA_CONFIRM_DELAY_SEC
	int "Auto-confirm delay (seconds)"
	default 120
	depends on MESHTASTIC_OTA_AUTOCONFIRM

endif # MESHTASTIC_OTA

config MESHTASTIC_SMP_CENTRAL
	bool "SMP (mcumgr) client over BLE: this node manages a peer node"
	depends on BT && BOOTLOADER_MCUBOOT
	select MCUMGR
	select NET_BUF
	select ZCBOR
	select CRC
	select SMP_CLIENT
	select MCUMGR_GRP_IMG_CLIENT
	select MCUMGR_GRP_OS_CLIENT
	select BT_CENTRAL
	select BT_GATT_CLIENT
	select FLASH_MAP
	help
	  The other side of overlay-ota-ble.conf. Zephyr has an SMP server over
	  BLE and an SMP client core, but no client TRANSPORT that talks to that
	  server from another Zephyr node. This adds one: the node connects as a
	  BLE central to a peer's SMP GATT service (the same service smpmgr --ble
	  uses) and runs the same img_mgmt / os_mgmt commands a laptop would —
	  upload, mark test, reset, confirm — so a node can update its neighbour
	  with no host in the middle. The peer needs no new firmware.

	  The image it pushes is whatever is staged in THIS node's slot1 (a
	  signed image uploaded there and never marked for test, which MCUboot
	  leaves alone) — the node is a courier. Shell: `smpc`.

if MESHTASTIC_SMP_CENTRAL

config MESHTASTIC_SMP_CENTRAL_JOB_STACK_SIZE
	int "Stack for the push/update job thread"
	default 4096
	help
	  The upload loop reads flash and drives img_mgmt_client (zcbor encode
	  into a net_buf, then a blocking wait per chunk). Internal RAM.

config MESHTASTIC_SMP_CENTRAL_JOB_PRIORITY
	int "Priority of the push/update job thread"
	default 10
	help
	  Preemptible and low: a firmware push is background work next to the
	  radio and the phone link.

endif # MESHTASTIC_SMP_CENTRAL

config MESHTASTIC_DEPOT
	bool "Firmware depot: a LittleFS of images for other nodes on the board's spare flash"
	depends on SOC_FAMILY_ESPRESSIF_ESP32
	# FILE_SYSTEM + FILE_SYSTEM_LITTLEFS come from the overlay: LittleFS's own
	# deps (FILE_SYSTEM_LIB_LINK, the module) do not resolve through a select.
	depends on FILE_SYSTEM_LITTLEFS
	select FLASH_MAP
	help
	  Mounts the board's `depot` partition (boards/heltec/.../heltec_partitions_16M.dtsi)
	  as LittleFS at /depot at boot, formatting it on first use. Images are put there
	  over SMP file management (`smpmgr file upload <bin> /depot/<name>`) and served
	  to a neighbour by the SMP client (`smpc push /depot/<name>`),
	  so a courier keeps its cargo across its own OTA — slot1 no longer doubles as the
	  hold. Needs the fstab node enabled: samples/meshtastic/depot.overlay.

config MESHTASTIC_FLEET_CLASS
	int "Fleet image class of this build (0 = unset)"
	range 0 255
	default 0
	help
	  A small operator-assigned number naming what this image is FOR: the
	  (board, build variant) pair — e.g. the XIAO BLE node, the Heltec R8
	  courier, the Heltec V4 transmit-disabled node. hw_model alone cannot say
	  it: one board runs several variants that must never replace each other.
	  A courier only offers a node an image of the node's own class, and a
	  node with class 0 is offered nothing. Shown by `meshtastic version`;
	  carried in the peer-link beat from version 2 of that frame.
